    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5503" root="جرذ" body-key="j">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جرّذ</span></b>  (tropical:)  <i>He trimmed</i> a tree, <i>as though by removing its</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَرَذ</span>, meaning its <i>faulty parts,</i> or
<i>knots,</i> which are likened to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِرْذَان</span> [pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُرَذٌ</span>]:
whence ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ مُجَرَّذٌ</span></b> . (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [And hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جرّذهُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الدَّهْرُ</span> (tropical:)  <i>Time,</i> or <i>fortune, tried and strengthened
him by means of experience in affairs.</i> (T, L,
TA.)

